Suggests: network-manager, tcpdump
Description: AirDrop and AWDL implementation for Linux
 opendrop-rs implements Apple Wireless Direct Link (AWDL) and the AirDrop
 application protocol on Linux. The filin command creates and bridges an awdl0
 interface using a monitor-mode Wi-Fi adapter, while luftlift discovers AirDrop
 peers and sends or receives files over the resulting IPv6 link.
 .
 filin requires CAP_NET_ADMIN and CAP_NET_RAW for normal operation, plus a
 Wi-Fi adapter and driver capable of monitor-mode frame injection.
